# Personal model overlay — copy this file to `configs/models.local.yaml` to use it.
#
# `configs/models.local.yaml` (note: NOT `.example`) is gitignored and merged into the
# shared manifest at kernel startup by ConfigBundle._merge_local_models(). It exists so one
# operator can route a model on their own machine WITHOUT touching configs/models.yaml —
# the file every community install of this project shares.
#
# Use this for a model that:
#   - carries a license this project's own bar (knowledge/research.md invariant 8) does not
#     clear for a shared default — e.g. a non-OSI vendor license with unusual terms you have
#     personally reviewed and accepted for your own use;
#   - is still under personal quality evaluation and you don't want it influencing anyone
#     else's install;
#   - is simply yours: a fine-tune, a checkpoint nobody else has, a local experiment.
#
# RULES, not suggestions:
#   1. A local model id can shadow (override) a manifest model id, but install-profiles.yaml
#      never references local-only ids, so `Install.ps1 -Profile core|workstation|full` can
#      never pull one in. Routing to it is only possible by explicit capability request.
#   2. `verified_source: true` still means what it means everywhere else in this project:
#      the source was actually checked, not merely typed. Verify it before setting it.
#   3. Put the REAL reasoning for accepting a non-default license in `license_note`, not just
#      "ok". If you ever hand this repository to someone else, `models.local.yaml` does not
#      travel with it (it's gitignored) — but the decision trail should still make sense to
#      you six months from now.
#   4. `status: candidate` (not `final`) is the right default for anything not yet
#      quality-evaluated: candidates only route in `mode: deep`, never fast/smart, so an
#      unevaluated personal model can't silently win a routing decision it hasn't earned.
#
# Worked example below — the actual entry used on this machine as of 2026-08-21, after
# measuring an 8.3x generation-speed win over the dense Qwen3.8-27B incumbent at essentially
# the same VRAM cost (docs/FIXES.md F-012) and accepting the NVIDIA Open Model License's
# Article 8 indemnification clause for personal use only (never for a shared profile).

models:
  - id: nemotron35-lightning-30b-a3b
    name: NVIDIA Nemotron 3.5 Lightning 30B-A3B
    source: nvidia/NVIDIA-Nemotron-3.5-Lightning-30B-A3B-BF16
    source_type: huggingface
    verified_source: true
    status: candidate
    install_policy: local
    capabilities:
      - reasoning
      - coding
      - planning
      - synthesis
      - verification
    preferred_engines:
      - llama_cpp
    quality_prior: 0.75
    resident_priority: 0
    estimated_vram_mb: 9438
    can_cpu_offload: true
    exclusive_gpu: true
    commercial_allowed: true
    license_note: >-
      NVIDIA Open Model License. Not OSI-approved; Article 8 requires the licensee to
      indemnify NVIDIA against third-party claims arising from the model, its derivatives,
      or its outputs. Accepted for PERSONAL/LOCAL use only on 2026-08-21. Never to be added
      to configs/models.yaml or any shared install profile. See docs/FIXES.md F-012/F-022
      and knowledge/research.md invariant 8 and D-012.
    notes: >-
      Sparse-active hybrid MoE (nemotron_h architecture; 128 experts, 6 active, ~3B active
      of 30B total). Measured 2026-08-21 on this machine: 52.79 tok/s generation at 9438 MiB
      peak VRAM with `-ncmoe 32` -- 8.3x the dense Qwen3.8-27B incumbent's 6.36 tok/s at
      essentially the same VRAM footprint. Quality on real coding/planning tasks is NOT yet
      evaluated; quality_prior above is a deliberately conservative placeholder, not a
      benchmarked claim. Requires the runtime's already-generated llama-server preset
      (state/llama-models.ini) to carry a matching [nemotron35-lightning-30b-a3b] section
      with `n-cpu-moe = 32` -- no engine alias is needed since the model id matches the
      preset section name exactly.
